HILDA AND THE TROLL

By Luke Pearson

SCENE 1 — THE CAMP

HILDA:
It's going to rain tonight! Can I sleep in the tent?

MOTHER:
Oh, you think so? As long as you—

Oh, look. You've gone and let the Wood Man in again!

HILDA:
What is this guy?

SCENE 2 — THE MORNING AFTER

HILDA (NARRATION):
Well, the wind shook the tent all night.

It was cold, wet—overall, pretty traumatic.

But such is the life of the adventurer.

SCENE 3 — HEADING UP THE HILL

HILDA:
Mother, I'm going to go up the hill for the day and do some drawing.

MOTHER:
Okay, sweetie. Be back for dinner.

And draw me something nice!

HILDA:
I'm drawing rocks!

SCENE 4 — THE WOOD MAN

HILDA:
What's with you? Why do you keep coming in here uninvited?

HILDA:
I still think he's very rude. And a weirdo too...

MOTHER:
Leave him be, Hilda. I think he comes to keep warm or something. And besides, he brings us wood.

SCENE 5 — THE ROCK

HILDA:
Poor thing. It must have drifted down the fjord and gotten lost.

Where'll he end up? I wonder if it matters...

HILDA (NARRATION):
By day, it's nothing but a peculiar-looking rock.

But by darkness...

It takes the form of a fierce and powerful troll!

SCENE 6 — PREPARING FOR THE TROLL

HILDA:
Luckily, I was prepared for this precise eventuality.

I need you to take this.

HILDA:
I must draw it.

I've never heard of them coming this far down the mountain before.

HILDA:
And tie it around his nose. That way, if he budges, we'll hear it.

Not that he—

HILDA:
Prepared, you know. Just in case a cloud goes over or something.

SCENE 7 — THE FOREST

HILDA:
Pretty sure that troll isn't finding us.

But we are in a big, scary forest...

And probably surrounded by all manner of weird creatures.

Kind of cool, huh?

HILDA:
I bet he knows where he's going.

SCENE 8 — LOST

HILDA:
Everyone goes the same...

We need to get out of here.

And soon.

There's no point...

If no one knows...

SCENE 9 — HELP

HILDA:
I knew it! We're saved!

I'm sure they won't mind if we let ourselves—

We are in distress!

SCENE 10 — RETURNING HOME

HILDA:
I still don't get it, though...

Why'd you come here when you have such a cool house?

TROLL:
Thanks a lot for bringing me home.

HILDA:
I'm aware of too much in my own house to ever be truly comfortable in it.

HILDA:
What a noteworthy day.

SCENE 11 — THE BELL

HILDA:
I'm ready.

HILDA:
Or I would be...

HILDA:
I think you have it.

According to this, trolls—

HILDA:
The bell trick is nowadays commonly accepted to be rather cruel.

HILDA:
See? Don't you read that far?

HILDA:
Well, that explains why he followed me here...

The poor thing can't reach.

He needs help getting it off!

SCENE 12 — FRIENDS

HILDA:
I knew trolls were nice!

HILDA:
Oh, I see. I'll draw you a—

HILDA:
You brought it all this way to give it back?!

HILDA:
Friends. Best friends!

HILDA:
I've always wanted to be friends.
